	spec: 'Hal keeps relevant plumbing visible once (AGENTS.md, tasks/README.md): tool cards show identifiers users act on, file paths, failures and the whole output, never call IDs, argument types or restated defaults, which stay in session files. Invalid and unfamiliar arguments and rejection reasons stay visible. Bash modifies accepts relative paths/globs without parent traversal and absolute paths/globs beneath /tmp, since allowed scratch writes must be declarable; other absolute paths, NULs, empty paths and non-string entries remain rejected before launch. Absolute /tmp literals and globs participate in snapshots, sensitive-file checks and canonical overlap locks, and retain absolute names in file-change records. Errors identify the invalid modifies entry and reason, give allowed path forms and state that the command did not run. Tool schema and SYSTEM.md explain these forms. Behavioral tests exercise absolute scratch snapshots/glob creation and invalid declarations. Scratch integration fixtures live explicitly beneath /tmp on macOS and Linux, independent of os.tmpdir or TMPDIR. Suite cleanup resets host state before restoring HAL_HOME and deleting the fixture, including after assertion failures.',
